<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2012/Flash-7.jpg" alt="A conformation portrait of a horse in the early stages" width="600" height="437" /></p>
<p>The hooves are now painted in, although only three are showing so far. &nbsp;I spent a full morning on them.</p>
<p>I worked on the body to build up the paint layer a little and it's starting to look more finished. &nbsp;I also wiped some extra tone into the background to give me a better sense of where to take it. &nbsp;My original vision for the portrait was to have the background largely unpainted, but I've decided it needs something more substantial so I will probably use some thin mid-tone grey to help define the horse.</p>